OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F303A1786061888
OL,3,CTeenagers overwhelmingly likely to
OL,4,Cturn off optional social media curfews
OL,5,C` poll
OL,7,FMost teenagers intend to opt out of
OL,8,Fthe Government's planned social media
OL,9,Fcurfews, polling has suggested.
OL,11,FSir Keir Starmer unveiled plans for a
OL,12,Fvoluntary curfew for 16 and 17-year-
OL,13,Folds in his final weeks in office.
OL,15,FThe curfew would prevent teenagers
OL,16,Faccessing social media sites between
OL,17,Fmidnight and 6am by default, but could
OL,18,Fbe turned off.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,304,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30302
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F303A1786061888
OL,3,CTeenagers overwhelmingly likely to
OL,4,Cturn off optional social media curfews
OL,5,C` poll
OL,7,FThe poll by Censuswide found 84.6% of
OL,8,F16-18-year-olds said they would opt
OL,9,Fout of the proposed curfews.
OL,11,FThe poll, conducted on behalf of the
OL,12,FOnline Responsibility Network, found
OL,13,F45.2% of teenagers said they would
OL,14,Fturn the curfew off to allow them to
OL,15,Fspeak to friends or family, while
OL,16,Fanother 37.2% would turn it off to
OL,17,Fwatch online content.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,304,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30303
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F303A1786061888
OL,3,CTeenagers overwhelmingly likely to
OL,4,Cturn off optional social media curfews
OL,5,C` poll
OL,7,FLeanne Proctor, regulatory lead at the
OL,8,FOnline Responsibility Network, said
OL,9,Fthe research suggests a curfew is
OL,10,F"unlikely to be enough on its own to
OL,11,Fprevent online harms".
OL,13,FShe said: "There is no single solution
OL,14,Fto protecting children online.
OL,26,@rD@AOUsD@UO]uD@KOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,304,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30304
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F303A1786061888
OL,3,CTeenagers overwhelmingly likely to
OL,4,Cturn off optional social media curfews
OL,5,C` poll
OL,7,F"Rather than relying on broad service-
OL,8,Flevel restrictions, greater focus
OL,9,Fshould be placed on design feature-
OL,10,Flevel protections and robust age
OL,11,Fassurance, helping to ensure young
OL,12,Fpeople have age-appropriate
OL,13,Fexperiences without unnecessarily
OL,14,Frestricting access."
OL,16,FAnnouncing the policy last month,
OL,17,Fministers also proposed turning of
OL,18,Faddictive features such as auto-
OL,19,Fscrolling and algorithmic feeds for
OL,20,Fyoung people.
OL,26,@oD@AOUvD@TO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
