CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F303A1786061888
OL,3,CTeenagers overwhelmingly likely to
OL,4,Cturn off optional social media curfews
OL,5,C` poll
OL,7,F"In our national poll, 64% of young
OL,8,Fpeople aged 16 to 21 supported
OL,9,Frestricting children from certain apps
OL,10,Fat night and our trials found
OL,11,Fovernight curfews quickly became part
OL,12,Fof daily routines and helped improve
OL,13,Fsleep and concentration.
OL,15,F"We are providing strong protections
OL,16,Fby default while giving 16 and 17-year-
OL,17,Folds the ability to decide whether
OL,18,Fthose protections fit their
OL,19,Fcircumstances, recognising they are
OL,20,Fcapable of making informed decisions."
OL,26,@oD@AOUwD@AOU|D@fO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/8
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
